# .agents/handoff-extra — this repository's own verification criteria
#
# Every handoff `scripts/runstate.sh handoff` writes ends with the plugin's
# verification contract: six generic REQUIRED lines from
# `templates/handoff-required.md`. Each non-blank, non-`#` line of THIS file is
# appended after those six as a further `REQUIRED` line, verbatim, and the
# reviewer holds the result file to it exactly as it holds it to the six.
#
# One criterion per line, phrased as a demand on the work — what must be done
# or shown, not advice to weigh. A line applies to every packet; there is no
# syntax for making one conditional. Lines from every discovered config root
# are unioned, so a nested repository can add criteria but never remove yours.
#
# Blank lines and lines beginning with `#` are ignored, so this file as shipped
# changes no handoff. Uncomment nothing; write your own.
#
# Examples of the kind of line that belongs here:
#
#   a change to money movement, balances or ledger state states the invariant
#   it preserves and the test that observes it holding
#
#   a change to a generated fixture regenerates it with the project's own
#   command and reports that command's output, never hand-edits the fixture
#
#   a schema change names the migration that accompanies it and the rollback
#   that was run against it
